{
  "id": "nord.stage-3",
  "maker": "Nord",
  "model": "Stage 3",
  "category": "keyboard",
  "summary": "A stage keyboard combining three independent sections - organ, piano and synth - playable as layers or splits. Everything connects on the rear apart from the pedals underneath it. Laid out here as a worked example of a device whose playing surface is its top rather than its front: the front of an 88 is the blank lip under the keys. The nine organ drawbars are drawn as drawbars; on the 88 and 76 they are LED drawbars driven by button pairs, so the drawing is a caricature of what the control does rather than of how it moves.",
